        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 5:03PM CDT by NWS Dodge City KS</headline>
        <description>At 503 PM CDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Belvidere, moving northeast at 30 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

This strong thunderstorm will be near...
Belvidere around 510 PM CDT.
Croft around 515 PM CDT.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
